Buttons/GoToEventsCalendar/Caption: Events Calendar
Buttons/GoToEventsCalendar/Hint: Go to Events Calendar Layout
Buttons/GoToEventsCalendar/Description: Open the Events Calendar layout without normal tiddlers.
Buttons/GoToTiddlersCalendar/Caption: Tiddlers Calendar
Buttons/GoToTiddlersCalendar/Hint: Go to Tiddlers Calendar Layout
Buttons/GoToTiddlersCalendar/Description: Open all tiddlers in an agenda or calendar using their date fields.
EventsCalendar/Sidebar/HelpMessage: You can add tiddlers with tag `$:/tags/EventCalendarSideBarSegment` to appear here (or install community plugins that have such tiddlers). Draggable content can be added to the entry like this: `<$draggable data-event='{ "duration": "01:00" }' data-tags="Tags">`. The `data-event` attribute can set information like duration for the event created by dragging, and the `data-tags` attribute can automatically add tags to the created event.
EventsCalendar/Sidebar/HelpMessageCreateButton: Click to create a calendar sidebar tiddler
EventsCalendar/Sidebar/ExampleNewTiddlerContent: `<$draggable data-event='{ "duration": "02:00" }' data-tags=" Tag1 Tag2">`* Drag me to calendar to create a new event with 2 hour duration and tags "Tag1" and "Tag2"`</$draggable>`
FrequentlyUsedTags/Caption: Frequently Used Tags
FrequentlyUsedTags/Description: Add tags to be displayed on the create event tiddler popup, so you can click on them to add tag to new tiddler quickly. Tags can have `caption` field as displayed name. And if tags here form a tag tree, they will be displayed as a tree.
FrequentlyUsedTags/EmptyPrefix: Go to
FrequentlyUsedTags/SettingsLink: Plugin Settings
FrequentlyUsedTags/EmptySuffix: in the control panel or plugin page to add frequently used tags.
Prefix/Caption: Prefix
Prefix/Description: Auto add prefix to all created event.
Appearance/Caption: Appearance
Appearance/24HourFormat: 24 Hour Format
Appearance/24HourFormatDescription: Show 24 hour format in calendar left slot label and events
Appearance/Timeline: Timeline
Appearance/TimelineDescription: Draw a vertical line on the left side of the agenda (list) view as a timeline.
Appearance/TimelineCheckbox: Enable by default
Appearance/FirstDay: First Day
Appearance/FirstDayDescription: First day of the week.
Appearance/SlotDuration: Slot Duration
Appearance/SlotDurationDescription: The frequency for displaying time slots.
Appearance/SearchPageLimit: Search Page Limit
Appearance/SearchPageLimitDescription: In search layout, the maximum number of events to display in the list. (Too large will have performance impact).
Appearance/WideScreenDefaultView: Wide Screen Default View
Appearance/WideScreenDefaultViewDescription: On desktop wide screens, use the wider week view or the three-day view that is convenient for comparing the left time.
Appearance/WideScreenDefaultView/ThreeDay: Three Day View
Appearance/WideScreenDefaultView/Week: Week View
Appearance/MobileEnabledButtons: Buttons Shown on Mobile
Appearance/MobileEnabledButtonsDescription: Mobile screens are small, and displaying too many buttons can cause UI crowding. However, if you need these buttons, you can enable them here. By default, only "Three Day", "Day", and "List" views are shown.
Appearance/MobileEnabledButtons/Month: month
Appearance/MobileEnabledButtons/Week: week
